# sprint_sec_fs_native_part3.oot — (Part 3 of sprint_sec_fs_native.oot)
# Continuation of `openOODA/audit/sprint_sec_fs_native.oot`.

---
HUNT 4 — OODA_FS_WRITEDIR still required by runtime
---

Still the write overlay. Not removed. Not optional. Fail-closed.

| C op | getenv | Deny when |
|------|--------|-----------|
| `oo_write_file` | `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` | unset / empty / `/` / not under (`chs_rt_fs.c:57-59`) |
| `oo_fs_remove_file` | same | L127-129 |
| `oo_fs_mkdir` | same | L137-139 |
| `oo_fs_hardlink` | same on **old and new** | L147-148 |
| `oo_fs_symlink` | same on **link and target** | L156-157 |

Policy read is `oo_process_policy_getenv` — key must be `OODA_` /
`OO_`. `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` matches. A renamed `FS_WRITEDIR` would
be NULL → deny all. Good fail-closed.

`path_under_writedir` (`chs_rt_fs.c:24-32`):

- both path and dir must be absolute
- dir `/` refused
- `realpath(dir)` must work (writedir must exist)
- existing path: `realpath(path)` prefix+boundary
- missing leaf: parent realpath + basename not `.`/`..`/`/`

`write_file` then `openat(O_NOFOLLOW)`. **mkdir / unlink / link /
symlink do not.** Overlay is necessary and insufficient.

### What still needs the env
Every native mutate used by this wave:

    fs_mkdir / fs_mkdir_p / sh_mkdir_p
    fs_write_file / fs_copy_file / fs_copy_tree / sh_copy
    fs_remove_file
    fs_hardlink / fs_symlink

Without the env, each `oo_*` returns Err `… denied: path not under
OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` (mkdir/write/remove wording). Scripts that only
hold FsWriteCap cannot write. That is the T3 6.4 contract. It is
still there.

### What the env does **not** cover
| Surface | Writedir? |
|---------|-----------|
| `read_file` / `path_exists` / `file_size` | **no** — any-path `fopen(path.data)` |
| `fs_read_dir` / `fs_is_dir` / `fs_walk` | **no** |
| `fs_copy_tree` **src** | **no** (read side) |
| `sh_clean` `rm -rf` | **no** |
| `sh_chmod` / git / tar / find / curl | **no** |
| `process_exec` generally | **no** |

So: native mkdir/copy **still need** the env to succeed at C.
`fs_mkdir_p` **hides** the need (Ok on deny). `sh_clean` **ignores**
the need (shell delete anywhere uid can unlink).

Hardlink residual (T3 W7) is still open: hardlink an outside file
into writedir, then `write_file` / copy dest overwrites the outside
inode. `path_under_writedir` on the writedir leaf is true.

### Check map vs runtime
`sealed_fs_kind_of` still only names

    read_file / fs_read / path_exists / file_size
    write_file / fs_write

It does **not** name `oo_fs_mkdir`, `fs_mkdir`, `oo_fs_remove_file`,
`oo_fs_read_dir`, `oo_fs_is_dir`, `oo_fs_hardlink`, `oo_fs_symlink`.

Runtime still `require_fswrite` / `require_fsread` on those C ops.
Check-path seal for the new names is a **gap**. User wrappers take
typed caps, so `fs_mkdir_p(fw, …)` still needs a Fw argument to
typecheck the call. A direct `oo_fs_mkdir` free call is not
preferred-kind denied the way `write_file` is. Runtime exits 1 on
a forged/missing token (`oo_cap_require_fswrite`). Do not call the
check map complete for native mkdir/copy.

CAPS.oot still says "FsWriteCap — write_file. Writes also obey
OODA_FS_WRITEDIR". mkdir/remove/copy are not in that sentence.
Doc lag, not a runtime drop.

---
ATTACK MATRIX (this wave only)
---

Verdict: BLOCK / BYPASS / LIE-OK / FAIL-CLOSED / residual.

| # | Attack | Want | Live |
|---|--------|------|------|
| M1 | mkdir_p when prefix is a file | Err | **LIE-OK** |
| M2 | mkdir_p outside writedir | Err | **LIE-OK** (C deny swallowed) |
| M3 | mkdir_p relative | deny or Err | **LIE-OK** |
| M4 | parent dir → symlink between allow and mkdir | deny | **residual TOCTOU** (no mkdirat) |
| M5 | mkdir 0777 | umask | **0777 request**; umask is host TCB |
| C1 | copy_tree src symlink → /etc | refuse or copy-link | **BYPASS copy-out** (Fr any-path) |
| C2 | copy_tree cycle symlink | refuse | **unbounded recurse** |
| C3 | copy_tree dest mkdir fail | Err | **LIE-OK** then child write fail / empty Ok |
| C4 | is_dir 1024 vs PATH_MAX write | one path | **truncate split** |
| C5 | sh_copy after gate | native + bound | native recurse + **same holes**; gate only charset |
| R1 | sh_clean `--no-preserve-root /` | refuse | **in-class**; GNU wipe |
| R2 | sh_clean `foo /` | one path | **in-class**; second operand |
| R3 | sh_clean `x; id` with gate | refuse | **BLOCK** (`;` not in class) |
| R4 | same if gate bypassed | refuse | **BYPASS RCE** |
| R5 | sh_clean `/tmp/out` with writedir=/tmp/wd | deny | **BYPASS** (no overlay) |
| W1 | native write/mkdir unset WRITEDIR | deny | **FAIL-CLOSED** at C |
| W2 | mkdir_p unset WRITEDIR | deny | **LIE-OK** at .oo |
| W3 | hardlink outside + write | deny | **BYPASS** (T3 W7 still) |
| W4 | write_file leaf symlink | deny | **BLOCK** openat O_NOFOLLOW |
| S1 | check `oo_fs_mkdir` without Fw | deny prefer Fw | **map miss** (runtime still require) |

No live dual-repro this turn. M1/M2/R1/C1 are code-path FN, not
paper.

---
RESIDUAL (do not close on paper)
---

- **mkdir_p always Ok.** File-in-the-way, writedir deny, relative,
  EACCES: discarded. `fs_copy_tree` err-check is dead. HIGH honesty.
- **mkdir TOCTOU / follow.** `mkdir(2)` after realpath; no
  `mkdirat`/`O_NOFOLLOW`. MED/HIGH, same family as T3 parent-dentry.
- **copy_tree follows symlinks, no cycle, no depth.** Copy-out +
  stack. HIGH. `fs_walk` residual is now a write amplifier.
- **is_dir 1024 vs PATH_MAX.** Silent truncate. MED.
- **sh_clean still `rm -rf` + ProcessCap.** No writedir. No Fw.
  In-class space/`-`/`/` wipe. Gate bypass restores `;` RCE.
  **CRITICAL** while any caller feeds a non-literal `dir`.
- **No rmdir / remove_tree.** DE10 item not landed. Clean cannot
  move without it (or a careful native walk+unlink that still
  needs a dir-remove op).
- **OODA_FS_WRITEDIR still required** at C for mkdir/write/remove/
  link/symlink. Unset still fail-closed. Facade mkdir_p **lies**
  about that. Clean **ignores** it.
- **Reads still any-path.** Copy src is the read hole.
- **Hardlink writedir escape** still open (T3 W7).
- **sealed_fs_kind_of** not extended to mkdir/remove/dir/is_dir.
  Runtime require holds; check preferred-kind does not.
- **sh_arg_ok smoke** does not cover space / leading `-` / `../` /
  `--no-preserve-root`. A green smoke is not this seal.
- **git/tar/chmod/find/curl/printenv** still shell. Not this hunt;
  still product API.

**Not path-A.** Native mkdir/copy is a ProcessCap→Fs* move plus a
Result lie. Clean is the same sink `sprint_sec_sh.oot` named.

## LEAVE-OFF
- `sh_mkdir_p` / `sh_copy` left the shell. Caps are Fw / Fr+Fw.
- `fs_mkdir_p` ignores every `fs_mkdir` Err and always returns Ok.
  File-in-the-way and writedir deny are silent. TOCTOU on `mkdir(2)`.
- `fs_copy_tree` recurses with `stat`/`opendir` follow, no cycle,
  no depth. mkdir_p lie is in the dest path.
- `sh_clean` is still `rm -rf ` + `dir` under ProcessCap. Gate
  allows space and `-`. Bypass restores classic `sh -c` inject.
- `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` is still required by runtime mutate. mkdir_p
  hides deny. clean never asks.

Do not edit product from this file. Do not green DE10.

